description
examples
Your text includes SpellingTool.DF.  The Spelling Tool complains about SpellingTool (what a fool!), and you do something about it.  Now the spelling tool complains about DF.  You don't want to insert DF into any wordlist; perhaps because it's so short that you worry about it's being too `near' real words.  You right-click MarkOK to mark it as being correct, and get on to some real words.
Better example:  Left-click Check gets you to the last name of your friend Simon Pastery.  You know from experience that you often misspell the word pastry as pastery, perhaps because you associate sweet rolls with your friend.  So you mark this use of Pastery as correct, but don't insert it in any wordlist.
